  "caption": "A road trip plus a long flight left Quinn with a grumpy back and a very stiff neck.\n\nOften it isn't the seat itself but the hours of staying still, so breaking up sitting tends to help more than chasing a perfect posture.\n\nSet up your car seat before you leave (knees slightly bent, a slight recline, a towel roll behind the lower back), stop about every two hours for a short walk, keep ankles and shoulders moving on flights, and lift luggage close with both hands and no twist.\n\nCalf pain, one swollen or warm leg, chest pain or breathlessness after travel need prompt medical care. Back pain that spreads below the knee with numbness or weakness is worth getting assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
